# Secret Handling

- Do not read files excluded by `.cursorignore` or `.gitignore` unless the user explicitly asks and confirms the risk.
- Do not add secrets, API keys, private keys, cookies, tokens, browser profiles, local databases, or production config to Git.
- Treat `.env`, `.env.development`, `.env.production`, `.env.local`, `.env.*.local`, `secrets/`, `.secrets/`, `private/`, and `credentials/` as sensitive.
- Committed `.env.example` files may contain only non-secret environment selectors or placeholders.
- If a secret may have been exposed, stop and tell the user to rotate or revoke it before continuing.

# Project Boundary

- Do not restore local Agent mode, Agent CLI, command execution entry points, background agents, multi-agent orchestration, or built-in image generation.
- Keep Nodora centered on the 14-step AI decision workflow.
- Do not bypass user confirmation before changing the main planning document or memory files.
